<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42041" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rūrĭcŏla</span></b> ,
		ae, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>adj. gen. omn.</i> [rus-colo], <i>that tills the
				ground; that lives in</i> or <i>belongs to the
				country</i>, <i>rural</i>, <i>rustic</i> (<b>poet.</b>); <i>masc.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">boves,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					5, 479</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. F. 1, 384</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phryges,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. M.
					11, 91</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Fauni,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 6, 392</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">deus,</span>”
				i.e. <i>Priapus</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Tr. 1, 10, 26</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dentes,</span>”
				i. e. <i>hoes</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					7, 859</span></i>
			.—<i>Fem.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ceres,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					Am. 3, 2, 53</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">formicula,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 6, p. 177</span></i>
			.—<i>Neutr.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aratrum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					Tr. 4, 6, 1</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rūrĭcŏ-la</span></b> ,
			ae, m.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(a).</b>
			<i>A tiller of the ground</i>, <i>a
				husbandman</i>, <i>countryman</i>, <i>rustic</i> (syn. colonus); plur.,
				<i><span class="en">Col.
				10, 337</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Nemes. Ecl. 1, 52</span></i>.
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(b).</b>
			<i>An ox</i> or <i>bull</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 15,
				124</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
